<!--Post: 5922--><!--Time: 1107457142-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5922"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The murders only had been linked to BTK after he claimed it, right? <BR> <BR>Maybe his disappearing through these years has something to do with him being convicted for some murder before he claimed it to be &#34;BTK큦 work&#34;. He might been arrested for one murder and WPD didnt realize that he had commited 8 &#40;or more&#41; murders before that one. <BR> <BR>It큦 not impossible, since, as many of us believe, he has commited more than 8 murders. <BR> <BR>WPD should research people arrested at that time or released shortly before BTK큦 first communication on 90큦.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5922-->
<!--Post: 5963--><!--Time: 1107467500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5963"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Trust me, they have. This is one of the first things you would do in an investigation after you have a profile of a suspect. You look for other possible murders with the same M.O. and after that you see which ones are solved and which ones are not and you see where the suspects are and were when the crimes were committed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5963-->
<!--Post: 6022--><!--Time: 1107482574-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I see. You&#39;re right. <BR> <BR>But I think about the possibility of other murders commited by this person not using BTK&#39;s modus operandi. <BR>Of course I am based much more on my beliefs than on facts, but I think BTK is like a character for this guy and not all of his killing were under this MO.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6022-->
<!--Post: 6034--><!--Time: 1107486606-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Doom<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Doom<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->LE has CODIS and AFIS...He was not in prison anywhere or in the military.  He could have been commited but I do not think so.  <BR> <BR>Doom<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6034-->
<!--Post: 6043--><!--Time: 1107490348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6043"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 8:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I researched Kasper for males that were  <BR>incarcerated from the late 80&#39;s through  <BR>2001-2004 between the ages of 63-66.  <BR>Could be a wild goose chase. Who knows the real  <BR>age, and who knows if he was ever locked up.  <BR> <BR>Kasper - Kansas Adult Supervised Population Electronic Repository  <BR> <BR>I did find one person that appears to reside in  <BR>Wichita, but I don&#39;t want to post anyone&#39;s info  <BR>here.  <BR> <BR>Took several hours to perform this search too.  <BR> <BR>You can search Kasper here:  <BR><a href="http://docnet.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/defaultz.asp" target=_top>http://docnet.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/defaultz.asp</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6043-->
<!--Post: 6214--><!--Time: 1107585118-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6214"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry... <BR>This link works better <BR><a href="http://docnet.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/" target=_top>http://docnet.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6214-->
<!--Post: 6564--><!--Time: 1107891877-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6564"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 11:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If BTK had been in prison during his absence 1986-2004, his DNA would be in the database. He definitely was not in prison. Some people say he got married or went on medication and that is what tamed him. Until something changed in his life and he resurfaced.  <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6564-->
<!--Post: 6579--><!--Time: 1107899003-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6579"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found this at a different site earlier. <BR><a href="http://www.kshb.com/" target=_top>http://www.kshb.com/</a> <BR> <BR>If you scroll down towards the bottom there&#39;s video called &#34;BTK Beyond The Killing&#34;. It also states that had BTK been in prison his DNA would have been on file. He may have been in a mental though. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6579-->
<!--Post: 7360--><!--Time: 1108423013-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7360"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Its highly unlikely the BTK Strangler was incarcerated between 1986 and 2004. He would not have the confidence to taunt the Wichita Police Department and the public for almost a year. The unknown subject is more likely to be in his early to mid 50s. The reference to being born in 1939 is an attempt to manipulate the police and public. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7360-->
